 ```
 
-Then in the body:
+No `include-in-header` script tag and no `filters:` entry are needed. Then in the body:
 
 ```markdown
-{{< motion-canvas ./animations/hexagons.js fullscreen=true loop=false >}}
-{{< motion-canvas ./animations/posit_footer.js auto fullscreen=true >}}
-{{< motion-canvas ./animations/kayak.js width="50%" >}}
+{{< canvas-commons ./animations/src/hexagons.js fullscreen=true loop=false >}}
+{{< canvas-commons ./animations/src/posit_footer.js fullscreen=true >}}
+{{< canvas-commons ./animations/src/kayak.js width=50% >}}
 ```
 
-Arguments seen in real decks: `fullscreen` (bare or `=true`), `background`, `loop=false`,
-`auto`, `width="50%"`.
-
-The two half-right failures:
-
-- Omit the `resources: dist/*/*` entry and the built JS is never copied to the output, so the
-  animation silently does not appear.
-- Omit the `include-in-header` script tag and `<motion-canvas-player>` is an undefined custom
-  element (inert, no error).
+Options: `fullscreen` (bare or `=true`), `background`, `loop=false`, `auto=false` (do not start when
+the slide is shown) and `width=50%` (ignored with `fullscreen`). Without `auto=false` the animation
+starts when its slide is shown. The old `{{< motion-canvas >}}` name still works but warns.
+
+The half-right failure is the `resources` entry. It must be `dist/**`: with `dist/*/*` the built
+scenes under `dist/animations/src/` are never copied to the output, so the animation silently does
+not appear once the deck is published.
 
 This is also the machinery behind the `animation:` title-slide metadata hook documented in
 `andrie-style.md`. Reach for it for a title-slide footer, a section-divider background, or one
 genuinely illustrative animation, not for decoration on every slide.
 
+To design that animation, use the `svg-to-motion-canvas` and `motion-canvas-authoring` skills,
+plus `motion-canvas-r-code` when it displays code, and `motion-canvas-scene` to bootstrap, upgrade
+or validate the project. For what each shortcode option really does, read
+`references/motion-canvas-shortcode.md`.
